{
  "_readme": [
    "Literal text in the design that is really data, mapped to a binding name.",
    "The importer replaces each exact (trimmed) text node with that binding, so",
    "studio-adapter.js can supply the real value.",
    "",
    "This is a patch over a design problem, not the fix. The proper fix is to make",
    "these bindings in the Claude Design project -- see DESIGN-GAPS.md. When that",
    "happens the literal stops appearing, the override stops matching, and",
    "`npm run design:import` reports it as unused so the entry can be deleted.",
    "",
    "Matching is exact on the trimmed string. An override that matches nothing is",
    "reported, never silently ignored.",
    "",
    "Note: the onboarding step numbers 1/2/3 are NOT data and must never be listed here.",
    "",
    "styleOverrides does the same for a literal `style` attribute that hardcodes data rather than appearance -- the new-job poster baked in a marketing image, so every lecture previewed with the same picture instead of its own thumbnail."
  ],
  "overrides": {
    "Youssef Channaoui": "accountName",
    "Studio · Salām, Youssef": "greeting",
    "3 connected · TikTok needs reconnecting": "connSummary",
    "Visa ending 4242 · expires 04/29": "cardLabel",
    "860 spent this month · resets nothing — tokens never expire": "spendSummary",
    "148 of 250 GB": "storageSummary",
    "112 GB": "storageSources",
    "34 GB": "storageClips",
    "2 GB": "storageTranscripts",
    "2 need you": "activityNeedsYou",
    "12 in total": "activityTotal",
    "From one 38-min talk": "emptySampleNote",
    "This is what one 38-minute lecture produces": "emptySampleCaption",
    "18": "weekPosted",
    "86": "weekMedian",
    "4": "weekHeld",
    "2h": "weekWorker",
    "13:00–15:00": "postWindow1",
    "18:00–19:30": "postWindow2",
    "21:00–23:00": "postWindow3",
    "Midday": "postWindowName1",
    "Evening": "postWindowName2",
    "Late": "postWindowName3",
    "42:11 · source lecture": "edSourceLabel",
    "09:14 / 42:11": "edTimeReadout",
    "Nasheed · Tala al-Badru": "edTrackName",
    "Soft choral hum": "edTrackNote",
    "of 42:11 — drag the top handle for the start, the bottom for the end.": "jobRangeHint",
    "He has the whole of the dunya": "capPreviewText",
    "≈ 20 hours of lecture processing, or about 62 rendered clips at your current settings.": "balanceMeans",
    "These numbers are sample output. On Pro, DeenAI reads your own clips, scores and posting record, and answers your questions — nothing here acts until then.": "aiDemoNote",
    "Unlock with Pro": "aiGateCta",
    "Desktop notifications": "notifsLabel"
  },
  "styleOverrides": {
    "position: relative; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; border-radius: 11px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid #26262A; background: #17171A url('src/public/marketing-assets/reel-kaaba-a.webp') center/cover no-repeat;": "jobPosterStyle",
    "position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 2px; width: 100%; accent-color: #D9B478; background: transparent; cursor: pointer;": "jobRangeStartStyle",
    "position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 2px; width: 100%; accent-color: #F0D6A6; background: transparent; cursor: pointer;": "jobRangeEndStyle"
  }
}
